{"id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#cor:chow-ii-dini-monotonicity","title":"cor:chow-ii-dini-monotonicity","path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles.md","line":229,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles.tex#cor:chow-ii-dini-monotonicity","uses":["[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles.tex","label":"cor:chow-ii-dini-monotonicity","line":470,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[monotonicity and exponential barriers]\n\\label{cor:chow-ii-dini-monotonicity}\n\\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-ii:page-0052}\n\\uses{lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound}\n\\dcref{ch10:10.25--10.26}\n\\group{Dini derivative tools}\n\n\nIf $d^+f/dt\\le0$ then $f$ is nonincreasing.  If $f(0)\\le0$ and\n$d^+f/dt\\le Cf$ whenever $f>0$, then $f\\le0$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\nApply the lemma to $f-f(t_0)$ for monotonicity, and to $e^{-Ct}f$ for the\nexponential assertion.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[monotonicity and exponential barriers] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a63686f772d69692d64696e692d6d6f6e6f746f6e6963697479\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-ii:page-0052</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch10-weak-maximum-principles%23lem%3Achow-ii-dini-upper-bound\">↗ lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch10:10.25–10.26</span></span>\\group Dini derivative tools <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d^+f/dt\\le 0$\">$d^+f/dt\\le 0$</span> then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> is nonincreasing. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f(0)\\le 0$\">$f(0)\\le 0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d^+f/dt\\le Cf$\">$d^+f/dt\\le Cf$</span> whenever <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f&gt;0$\">$f&gt;0$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f\\le 0$\">$f\\le 0$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Apply the lemma to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f-f(t_0)$\">$f-f(t_0)$</span> for monotonicity, and to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e^{-Ct}f$\">$e^{-Ct}f$</span> for the exponential assertion. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group、sketch"]},"previous":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound","next":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#lem:chow-ii-spatial-maximum-dini","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound","title":"lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound","label":"lem:chow-ii-dini-upper-bound"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#cor:chow-ii-heat-wmp","title":"cor:chow-ii-heat-wmp","label":"cor:chow-ii-heat-wmp"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch10-weak-maximum-principles#thm:chow-ii-continuous-set-wmp","title":"thm:chow-ii-continuous-set-wmp","label":"thm:chow-ii-continuous-set-wmp"},{"kind":"uses"